---
description: Documentation truthfulness and project-state maintenance
globs: "docs/**/*.md, README.md, SECURITY.md, LIMITATIONS.md, FEEDBACK.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Documentation

- Describe only behavior verified in the current repository or deployment.
- Use exact labels: implemented, tested, deployed, simulated, planned, or blocked.
- Link sponsor integrations to exact source files and public evidence.
- Never publish secrets, complete authorization material, or unredacted sensitive provider responses.
- Keep setup commands reproducible from a clean checkout.
- Record architectural decisions and their tradeoffs in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
- Update `docs/STATUS.md` after each phase; do not use README as a scratchpad.
- Keep `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/API_CONTRACTS.md`, and implementation types consistent.
- Add a dated note when an external SDK or API assumption is verified.

